        "procedure": "Under dry, oxygen-free argon in a glove-box, 12.8 mmol (0.500 g) K was dissolved in 16 ml of 1:1 (v:v) HOPri:toluene, followed by drop-wise addition of 0.85 ml of 1 M H2O (0.85 mmol) in HOPri:toluene (1:1 v:v). Then 4.263 mmol (1.000 g) LaCl3 was added and allowed to react for 48 h at room temperature. The mixture was centrifuged to remove white KCl. Evaporation of the solvent afforded crystals of 1.",
